   "why": [
    "Wheels are ruled out across their whole range: r=4.5 still cannot climb 5.45 cm or span 9 cm. Rocker-bogie would need about 6 cm wheels and stand about 14 cm tall, failing the 9 cm sofa. Tracks with a 6 cm idler climb the 5.45 cm step, and the track's top is at 7.5 cm, under the sofa. A 26 cm contact length bridges about 11.7 cm, more than the 9 cm trench. The long patch should cut ground pressure to a few hundred Pa, about 0.4 cm of sinkage. Ride height 2.5 keeps the tub top at 6.5 cm. Inner width 13 cm tries to also pass the bedroom door and the 28 cm gate. A 12 Wh pack offsets the tracks' higher energy per metre at about 0.56 m/s, so the lawn might also pass. Cost: $14 track kit plus one $2.50 AA cell, 4 days, 57 printer minutes."
